<title>UK: EX-DIVIDENDS TAKE 15.461 POINTS OFF FTSE 100 INDEX.</title>
<headline>EX-DIVIDENDS TAKE 15.461 POINTS OFF FTSE 100 INDEX.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stocks will go ex-dividend on Monday and the effect the effect will be to take 15.461 points off the index in early trading.</p>
<p>						 DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>						 (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>COMPANY					  Net	 Net</p>
<p>* Abbey National			   10.20	0.822</p>
<p>* B.A.T. Industries			10.00	1.772</p>
<p>* British Petroleum Co.		   5.50	1.794</p>
<p>* British Telecommunications     (a) 11.95	4.363</p>
<p>* Glaxo Wellcome		     (b) 15.00	3.051</p>
<p>* Lloyds TSB Group			  5.30	1.629</p>
<p>* National Westminster Bank	    10.60	1.036</p>
<p>* Siebe				  (b)  9.80	0.283</p>
<p>* TI Group			     (b)  5.10	0.139</p>
<p>* Tomkins				     8.39	0.573</p>
<p>(a) A special dividend of 35p will also be made by British Telecommunications.</p>
<p>(b) Dividend amounts for Glaxo Wellcome, Siebe and TI Group are Foreign Income Dividends (FIDs) only.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
